  "_meta": {
    "what": "Job 7's opponent ladder. One BRACKET per set. Nothing in here names the set it unlocks or its own position — buildLadder() in src/progress.js derives both from the live-set order, so a bracket for a set that is not live simply does not appear, and a live set with no bracket here gets a generated one automatically. Adding Team Rocket is adding a key, or adding nothing at all.",
    "authored": "2026-08-12, Job 7a.",
    "deck refs": "'theme:NAME' is DECKS in cards.js (data/decks.json). 'gbc:KEY' and 'jungle:NAME' are OPPONENT_DECKS (data/gbc_decks.json, data/jungle_decks.json). 'generate' is a pool spec handed to deckgen at match time, seeded off the opponent id so the same challenger always brings the same deck.",
    "names": "GBC characters keep their real names. Anything marked placeholder:true is ours and is meant to be replaced — Trevor's note, 12 Aug 2026: the decks and names are easily reshapable, the structure is what has to be right.",
    "ronald": "Ronald is the recurring rival, one deck per bracket in the order the GBC escalates them. His fourth, ronald_legendary, is the post-boss challenge in the last authored bracket; when a fourth set goes live it should probably move to being that bracket's boss instead.",
    "unassigned": "No GBC deck is unused. All 16 appear exactly once.",
    "base1 roster": "2026-08-19, Job 10.5. Trevor's eight Base Set decks (data/base1_decks.json) replaced the GBC placeholders: four theme decks as the T1 intro, five T2, two T3 gate, and the T4 as the boss. Built to OPPONENTS.md's tier spec — see ROSTERS.md for what decksim measured. NAMES AND TITLES ARE STILL OURS and marked placeholder:true; the decks are not. Ronald's first deck moved to base1's `extra`, so he is now the post-boss challenger rather than the boss, and the four club masters he shared a bracket with joined the other four in base2."
  },
